      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "# The Data Process\n",
        "\n",
        "The next section follows the step by step evaluation, cleaning, and encoding of the Freddie Mac Data. The example shown uses 2018 Q1. The same logic was then placed into an automated script so the other quarters and years could be standardized into the same final format.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Data Load & Clean- Origination"
      ],
      "id": "1ee45343"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "cache": true
      },
      "source": [
        "#| echo: true\n",
        "#| eval: true\n",
        "#| error: false\n",
        "#| warning: false\n",
        "\n",
        "#-- data load-- including NA values mentioned in dictionary\n",
        "or_2018= pd.read_csv(\"~/projects/data/homeloanadvisor/historical_data_2018Q1.txt\", sep=\"|\", header=None, na_values=[\"\", \"9999\", \"999\", \"9\", \"   \", \"X\"], low_memory=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "#-- column names--\n",
        "or_2018.columns= [\"credit_score\", \"first_payment_date\", \"first_time_buyer\", \"maturity_date\", \"msa\", \"mi_percent\", \"num_units\", \"occupancy\", \"cltv\", \"dti\", \"upb\", \"ltv\", \"or_interest_rate\", \"channel\", \"ppm\", \"amortization\", \"prop_state\", \"prop_type\", \"zipcode\", \"loan_id\", \"loan_purpose\", \"or_loan_term\", \"num_borrowers\", \"seller\", \"servicer\", \"super_conforming\", \"pre_harp_loan_id\", \"program_indicator\", \"harp_indicator\", \"prop_valuation\", \"interest_only\", \"mi_cancel\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "#-- date features--\n",
        "first_payment= pd.to_datetime(or_2018[\"first_payment_date\"], format=\"%Y%m\", errors=\"coerce\")\n",
        "maturity= pd.to_datetime(or_2018[\"maturity_date\"], format=\"%Y%m\", errors=\"coerce\")\n",
        "\n",
        "or_2018[\"first_payment_year\"]= first_payment.dt.year\n",
        "or_2018[\"first_payment_month\"]= first_payment.dt.month\n",
        "or_2018[\"maturity_year\"]= maturity.dt.year\n",
        "or_2018[\"maturity_month\"]= maturity.dt.month"
      ],
      "id": "3dc936f6",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "For our application we will drop several variables. The HARP program helped borrowers refinance their home when their home's value was less than their mortgage.[^1] The data points that identify with HARP will also be dropped because the data points represent a borrower that would not typically meet Freddie Mac's regular qualifications. Zip code will be dropped because its high cardinality is not worth keeping. We can use `msa` later for a metro or non-metro flag. `cltv` will be dropped because it is highly similar to `ltv`. We'll keep `loan_id` as a join key.\n",
        "\n",
        "[^1]: <https://www.fhfa.gov/news/fact-sheet/home-affordable-refinance-program-harp>"
      ],
      "id": "c5dccf4b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "cache": true
      },
      "source": [
        "#| echo: true\n",
        "#| eval: true\n",
        "#| error: false\n",
        "#| warning: false\n",
        "\n",
        "#-- removing HARP--\n",
        "or_2018= or_2018[or_2018[\"harp_indicator\"].isna()].copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "#-- dropping irrelevant variables--\n",
        "drop= [\"pre_harp_loan_id\", \"amortization\", \"harp_indicator\", \"program_indicator\", \"seller\", \"servicer\", \"first_payment_date\", \"maturity_date\", \"zipcode\", \"cltv\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "or_2018= or_2018.drop(columns=drop)"
      ],
      "id": "fb6d62bc",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Encoding\n",
        "\n",
        "The data dictionary provided by Freddie Mac specifies what the missing values are. The `msa` variable, for example, has missing values that may mean a property is not in a metropolitan area, or may actually mean \"unknown\". Zip code data appears in every entry, so imputation is possible using overlap. But a simpler and more reliable approach is to code a new variable using the `msa` column as binary: metro area or not."
      ],
      "id": "c1e74ffb"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#-- msa to metro area binary--\n",
        "or_2018[\"metro_area\"]= or_2018[\"msa\"].notna().astype(int)\n",
        "or_2018= or_2018.drop(columns=\"msa\")"
      ],
      "id": "c65b28c2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "There are columns with low cardinality that cannot be coded as binary but are better served by one-hot encoding."
      ],
      "id": "9d61440a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#-- categorical encoding--\n",
        "categorical_cols= [\"first_time_buyer\", \"loan_purpose\", \"prop_type\", \"occupancy\", \"channel\", \"num_units\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "or_2018[categorical_cols]= or_2018[categorical_cols].fillna(\"Unknown\")\n",
        "or_2018= pd.get_dummies(or_2018, columns=categorical_cols, drop_first=True, dtype=int)"
      ],
      "id": "d8ae3d82",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Numerical variables such as `ltv` and `credit_score` are skewed and will be imputed using the median. The median imputation will be completed during the data build so every quarter of the Freddie Mac datasets is complete. The modeling report will not need to repeat this imputation for the same standardized files."
      ],
      "id": "9c752e86"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#-- numeric imputation--\n",
        "numeric_impute= [\"credit_score\", \"dti\", \"ltv\", \"mi_percent\", \"prop_valuation\", \"upb\", \"or_interest_rate\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "or_2018[numeric_impute].skew()\n",
        "\n",
        "for col in numeric_impute:\n",
        "    or_2018[col]= or_2018[col].fillna(or_2018[col].median())"
      ],
      "id": "3cb1468a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Variables that are not useful for the app or standardized modeling file will be dropped. These variables are removed consistently so every quarterly dataset follows the same final set up."
      ],
      "id": "84e57f53"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#-- dropping low-value variables--\n",
        "or_2018[[\"ppm\", \"super_conforming\", \"interest_only\"]].nunique()\n",
        "or_2018= or_2018.drop(columns=[\"ppm\", \"super_conforming\", \"interest_only\"])"
      ],
      "id": "62c3706c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Data Clean Final Check"
      ],
      "id": "1e734fa3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| layout-ncol: 2\n",
        "\n",
        "#-- missing check--\n",
        "missing_check= or_2018.isna().sum().sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
        "missing_check[missing_check > 0]\n",
        "\n",
        "#-- shape check--\n",
        "or_2018.shape"
      ],
      "id": "971995e5",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The data is clean and ready to be joined to the target created from the monthly performance data. The same cleaning process will be placed into a function so it can be applied to all origination datasets coming from Freddie Mac's standardized files.\n",
        "\n",
        "------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "## Data Load & Clean- Performance"
      ],
      "id": "fc431866"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| error: false\n",
        "#| warning: false\n",
        "\n",
        "#-- performance load--\n",
        "perf_2018= pd.read_csv(\"~/projects/data/homeloanadvisor/historical_data_time_2018Q1.txt\", sep=\"|\", header=None, na_values=[\"\", \"9999\", \"999\", \"   \", \"X\"], low_memory=False)"
      ],
      "id": "80dbf6f6",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "For the performance file, `\"9\"` was not included in the missing value list because `zero_balance_code = 9` is a real category. It represents REO disposition."
      ],
      "id": "99576c4d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#-- performance column names--\n",
        "perf_2018.columns= [\"loan_id\", \"report_period\", \"current_upb\", \"delinquency_status\", \"loan_age\", \"remaining_months\", \"defect_settlement_date\", \"modification_flag\", \"zero_balance_code\", \"zero_balance_effective_date\", \"current_rate\", \"current_deferred_upb\", \"ddlpi\", \"mi_recoveries\", \"net_sales_proceeds\", \"non_mi_recoveries\", \"expenses\", \"legal_costs\", \"maintenance_costs\", \"taxes_insurance\", \"misc_expenses\", \"actual_loss\", \"modification_cost\", \"step_modification_flag\", \"deferred_payment_plan\", \"eltv\", \"zero_balance_removal_upb\", \"delinquent_accrued_interest\", \"disaster_delinquency\", \"borrower_assistance\", \"current_month_mod_cost\", \"interest_bearing_upb\"]"
      ],
      "id": "77a8d270",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Only the fields needed to construct the target variable and summarize the loan termination outcome were kept. The performance file contains repeated monthly rows for each loan, so it cannot be merged directly to the origination file without creating duplicate loan rows."
      ],
      "id": "c63a31cc"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#-- keeping needed performance variables--\n",
        "keeping= [\"loan_id\", \"report_period\", \"delinquency_status\", \"zero_balance_code\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "perf_2018= perf_2018[keeping].copy()"
      ],
      "id": "9403bf8d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Encoding\n",
        "\n",
        "The categorical variables will be mapped for interpretation. `zero_balance_code` is mapped to a readable label, while `delinquency_status` is converted into the target variable."
      ],
      "id": "78630040"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#-- delinquency map--\n",
        "delinquency_map= {\n",
        "    \"0\": \"Current or <30 Days Delinquent\",\n",
        "    \"1\": \"30-59 Days Delinquent\",\n",
        "    \"2\": \"60-89 Days Delinquent\",\n",
        "    \"3\": \"90-119 Days Delinquent\",\n",
        "    \"4\": \"120-149 Days Delinquent\",\n",
        "    \"5\": \"150-179 Days Delinquent\",\n",
        "    \"6\": \"180-209 Days Delinquent\",\n",
        "    \"RA\": \"REO Acquisition\"\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "#-- zero balance map--\n",
        "zero_balance_map= {\n",
        "    1.0: \"Prepaid or Matured\",\n",
        "    2.0: \"Third Party Sale\",\n",
        "    3.0: \"Short Sale or Charge Off\",\n",
        "    9.0: \"REO Disposition\",\n",
        "    15.0: \"Whole Loan Sale\",\n",
        "    16.0: \"Reperforming Loan Securitization\",\n",
        "    96.0: \"Defect Prior to Termination\"\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "perf_2018[\"zero_balance_label\"]= perf_2018[\"zero_balance_code\"].map(zero_balance_map).fillna(\"Not Applicable\")"
      ],
      "id": "f00ea03d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "We'll use the industry standard \"90+ days delinquent\". The goal is to estimate the probability that a loan becomes 90 or more days delinquent at any point during the observed performance history."
      ],
      "id": "2a05ff60"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#-- target: any 90+ days delinquent--\n",
        "dq_num= pd.to_numeric(perf_2018[\"delinquency_status\"].replace({\"RA\": 99}), errors=\"coerce\")\n",
        "\n",
        "target= (\n",
        "    dq_num\n",
        "    .groupby(perf_2018[\"loan_id\"])\n",
        "    .max()\n",
        "    .ge(3)\n",
        "    .astype(int)\n",
        "    .reset_index(name=\"any_90_dpd\")\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "c6cf1861",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The category `RA` is defined in the dictionary as REO acquisition. These loans will be treated as 90+ days delinquent because REO acquisition reflects a severe default or foreclosure outcome. `zero_balance_code` will be useful because it tells why a loan was closed or terminated, but it will not be used as a predictor variable in the final model. It is retained for app interpretation and audit use."
      ],
      "id": "a4f27482"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#-- last observed termination code per loan--\n",
        "zero_bal= (\n",
        "    perf_2018[perf_2018[\"zero_balance_code\"].notna()]\n",
        "    .sort_values([\"loan_id\", \"report_period\"])\n",
        "    .groupby(\"loan_id\")[\"zero_balance_code\"]\n",
        "    .last()\n",
        "    .reset_index()\n",
        "    .rename(columns={\"zero_balance_code\": \"termin_code\"}))\n",
        "\n",
        "#-- joining--\n",
        "target= target.merge(zero_bal, on=\"loan_id\", how=\"left\")\n",
        "\n",
        "#-- fill loans with no observed termination event--\n",
        "target[\"termin_code\"]= target[\"termin_code\"].fillna(0)\n",
        "\n",
        "#-- final join--\n",
        "final_2018= or_2018.merge(target, on=\"loan_id\", how=\"inner\")\n",
        "\n",
        "#-- csv checkpoint--\n",
        "final_2018.to_csv(\"~/projects/data/homeloanadvisor/model_input_2018Q1.csv\", index=False)"
      ],
      "id": "2387c6e0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Final Check"
      ],
      "id": "a6a63c4c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#-- final check--\n",
        "final_2018[\"loan_id\"].duplicated().sum()\n",
        "final_2018.shape\n",
        "final_2018[\"any_90_dpd\"].value_counts(normalize=True)"
      ],
      "id": "5bcc77d4",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "## State Default Rate\n",
        "\n",
        "A borrower's property state could help output an estimate of mortgage risk because delinquency rates can vary by location. However, if state-level default rates are calculated using the entire dataset, the feature would be considered data leakage. To avoid this, state default rates were calculated using the train split, then mapped onto the train and test data."
      ],
      "id": "cb659199"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#-- train test split--\n",
        "train_, test_= train_test_split(\n",
        "    final_2018,\n",
        "    test_size=0.3,\n",
        "    random_state=212,\n",
        "    stratify=final_2018[\"any_90_dpd\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "train_= train_.copy()\n",
        "test_= test_.copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "#-- state default rate on train only--\n",
        "state_def_rate= (\n",
        "    train_\n",
        "    .groupby(\"prop_state\")[\"any_90_dpd\"]\n",
        "    .mean()\n",
        "    .reset_index(name=\"state_def_rate\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "#-- fallback rate for unseen states--\n",
        "global_def_rate= train_[\"any_90_dpd\"].mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "#-- mapping train-only proportions to states--\n",
        "state_lookup= dict(zip(state_def_rate[\"prop_state\"], state_def_rate[\"state_def_rate\"]))\n",
        "\n",
        "train_[\"state_def_rate\"]= train_[\"prop_state\"].map(state_lookup)\n",
        "test_[\"state_def_rate\"]= test_[\"prop_state\"].map(state_lookup).fillna(global_def_rate)"
      ],
      "id": "9eda405d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The `prop_state` variable is removed after the state-level default rate is created. `loan_id` is removed because its an identifier, and `termin_code` is removed because it represents information observed after origination."
      ],
      "id": "3dd28cdd"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#-- removing identifier and audit columns--\n",
        "train_= train_.drop(columns=[\"loan_id\", \"prop_state\", \"termin_code\"], errors=\"ignore\")\n",
        "test_= test_.drop(columns=[\"loan_id\", \"prop_state\", \"termin_code\"], errors=\"ignore\")\n",
        "\n",
        "#-- csv checkpoint--\n",
        "train_.to_csv(\"~/projects/data/homeloanadvisor/train2018.csv\", index=False)\n",
        "test_.to_csv(\"~/projects/data/homeloanadvisor/test2018.csv\", index=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "state_def_rate.to_csv(\"~/projects/data/homeloanadvisor/state_def_rate_2018Q1.csv\", index=False)"
      ],
      "id": "28d4f662",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "------------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
        "\n",
        "## Automated Setup Script\n",
        "\n",
        "The 2018 Q1 process was converted into a Python script so the same cleaning logic could be applied to every available quarter and year. The script processes the raw Freddie Mac files, creates quarter-level files, combines all available quarters, and saves final modeling files.\n",
        "\n",
        "```{bash}\n",
        "#| eval: false\n",
        "\n",
        "cd ~/rstudio/DATA622-HomeLoanAdvisor\n",
        "python build_model_data.py\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "The automated script creates the final files used in the modeling section."
      ],
      "id": "ddc7ecb9"
    },
    {
